begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(-2{x}^{2}-9)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-9{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2}-9\\cdot x{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{(2)^{3}}{3}-0)-9(2-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{16}{3}-18 \\\\  & =-\\frac{70}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\frac{70}{3}.$" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309569 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309570 13194139534777 true] [17592186309569 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309571 13194139534777 true] [17592186309569 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309572 13194139534777 true] [17592186309569 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309573 13194139534777 true] [17592186309569 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309574 13194139534777 true] [17592186309569 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534777 true] [17592186309569 1041 "selection" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309569 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309570 13194139534777 true] [17592186309569 1110 #uuid "2a194efa-80ce-531b-82f0-16cf467051a0" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309570 1034 "\\frac{70}{3}" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309570 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534777 true] [17592186309570 1111 #uuid "f7b46985-9a46-5801-bcf5-15fb87e5681d" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309571 1034 "\\frac{29}{3}" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309571 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534777 true] [17592186309571 1111 #uuid "37419c56-6fb0-588f-bf63-d1e487b163f2" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309572 1034 "\\frac{29}{26}" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309572 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534777 true] [17592186309572 1111 #uuid "a47dfcf8-e777-54a5-aebd-1db7745eead3" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309573 1034 "45" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309573 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534777 true] [17592186309573 1111 #uuid "91d71b58-f11b-57fa-8df5-1fdeeb3f14e8" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309574 1034 "\\frac{38}{3}" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309574 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534777 true] [17592186309574 1111 #uuid "d5b027f7-6f6e-5102-9f7b-550dc3c1a467" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309575 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309576 13194139534777 true] [17592186309575 1089 "q-316226" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309575 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534777 true] [17592186309575 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/0a7a32f856d63403d7125f1c6bb9acc9a5fcd182c2f7fbd3f3ebdfa42f9c9c2c.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ between the curve $y=-{x}^{2}-8$, the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=2$ (shown above). Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$ \n{{field-1}}" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309575 1113 #uuid "b9764ba6-cf4b-5320-9e3f-a842856afa37" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309575 1145 "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(-{x}^{2}-8)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-8{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2}-8\\cdot x{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{(2)^{3}}{3}-0)-8(2-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{3}-16 \\\\  & =-\\frac{56}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is \n\n$$\nA=-{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{56}{3}.\n$$" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309576 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309577 13194139534777 true] [17592186309576 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309578 13194139534777 true] [17592186309576 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534777 true] [17592186309576 1041 "field-1" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309576 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309577 13194139534777 true] [17592186309576 1110 #uuid "4077d12f-bff4-5de2-8aa1-b365b80dc5aa" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309577 1034 "\\frac{56}{3}" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309577 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534777 true] [17592186309577 1111 #uuid "6674705c-28a3-562c-8bd1-67e3f13e2907" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309578 1034 "16" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309578 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534777 true] [17592186309578 1111 #uuid "9f091ad2-6197-5914-b32b-7ed6a917757b" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309579 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309580 13194139534777 true] [17592186309579 1089 "q-345385" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309579 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534777 true] [17592186309579 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/d43d7419f631b479478641ac203c6816693c68ffc40ccc1d4a8a72da0a03461a.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}}}$, the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{3}{2}$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309579 1113 #uuid "74326dd3-adad-5326-940c-9aa17cfe09b0" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309579 1145 "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3/2}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{3/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =arccos\\,(\\frac{x}{3}){|}_{0}^{3/2} \\\\  & =arccos\\,(\\frac{1}{2})-arccos\\,(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is \n\n$$\nA=-{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\n$$" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309581 13194139534777 true] [17592186309580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309582 13194139534777 true] [17592186309580 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534777 true] [17592186309580 1041 "field-1" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309580 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309581 13194139534777 true] [17592186309580 1110 #uuid "5f95d24b-f17d-5e37-a862-0fa05284d956" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309581 1034 "\\frac{\\pi}{6}" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309581 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534777 true] [17592186309581 1111 #uuid "4af8112b-bd64-5411-a7e7-7a66654158ba" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309582 1034 "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309582 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534777 true] [17592186309582 1111 #uuid "c946f0a9-5deb-55c3-8603-752ca595fc45" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309583 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309584 13194139534777 true] [17592186309583 1089 "q-73327" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309583 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534777 true] [17592186309583 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/70a4f7ef7589f303924f1c48e7b0c26cd2173960847ac660199d11ae144c0afc.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$, the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$, as shown above. Find the area of the region." 13194139534777 true] [17592186309583 1113 #uuid "7fd92209-d3be-59fd-82d6-ee543e246f84" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309583 1145 "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡0) \\\\  & =-(\\sqrt{2}-1) \\\\  & =1-\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\sqrt{2}-1.$" 13194139534777 true] [17592186309584 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309585 13194139534777 true] [17592186309584 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309586 13194139534777 true] [17592186309584 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309587 13194139534777 true] [17592186309584 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309588 13194139534777 t